# November 28, 2026: Carnegie libraries of Arizona, New Mexico and Hawaii: a batch of the pass the owner asked for to put the
# buildings Andrew Carnegie paid for on the map. Wikipedia's lists give four in Arizona, three in New Mexico and one in Hawaii,
# all public libraries; none of the three states had an academic Carnegie library. None was on the Atlas before, and no Atlas
# place within 1.5 km of any of them shares its name.
# Sources opened in this session: Wikipedia's lists of Carnegie libraries in Arizona, New Mexico and the United States (Hawaii's
# list leads to the State Library's article) and its articles; National Register records and nominations (the Park Service:
# Phoenix, Prescott, Las Vegas's Library Park district); SAH Archipedia (Phoenix, Tucson, Honolulu); the Pima County Public
# Library's early history; the Downtown Tucson Partnership; the Sharlot Hall Museum's Days Past article on Prescott's library;
# the Yuma County Library District's Heritage Library page; the City of Las Vegas's library page and notices; the New Mexico
# State Library's note on Raton; the Hawaii State Public Library System's branch page and history.
# Pins: ArcGIS geocoder points for street addresses, OpenStreetMap points for the Las Vegas library and Raton's Ripley Park;
# every pin looked at on the aerial.
from data_b import N
from data_ma import W
