# ---------------- Hawaii ----------------
N('hawaii-state-library-honolulu','Hawaii State Library (Library of Hawaii)','Honolulu','hi','civic','standing',21.30577,-157.85773,'exact','open','walk','','1911–1913',
  "Before it, Honolulu's books were kept by the Honolulu Library and Reading Room Association, founded in 1879 and given money and books by King Kalākaua, Queen Kapiʻolani, Queen Emma and Princess Bernice Pauahi Bishop. The ground was once Hāliʻimaile, the home of Boki and Liliha and later of Victoria Kamāmalu. Carnegie gave $100,000 (granted November 29, 1909, says Wikipedia's list), and the territory added $27,000. Henry D. Whitfield drew it; the cornerstone was laid on October 21, 1911, and it opened on February 1, 1913, with Edna Allyn as head librarian. C. W. Dickey's wings of 1928 to 1930 tripled its size round an open courtyard, and a large rear wing was added in 1990 to 1992. It is the main library of Hawaii's statewide public library system, in the Hawaii Capital Historic District, on the National Register since 1978.",
  "The front keeps the 1913 classical box, with a twenty-foot entrance porch of Tuscan columns and bronze doors and windows. Inside are a two-storey skylit lobby, cast-iron stacks holding a mezzanine, and the Edna Allyn children's room with Juliette May Fraser's murals of Hawaiian legends of 1934 and 1935. Hiroki Morinoue's mosaic Ocean Currents is in the courtyard floor, and Barbara Hepworth's bronzes Parent I and Young Girl stand on the front lawn. In November 2026 part of a ceiling over a courtyard walkway fell, and the courtyard and the gallery above it were shut until repairs are done.",
  '','478 South King Street, beside ʻIolani Palace and the State Capitol, downtown. The library has no parking of its own; parking nearby is metered. Hours from the library system\'s page.',
  [['Hawaii State Public Library System: Hawaii State Library','https://www.librarieshawaii.org/branch/hawaii-state-library/'],['Hawaii State Public Library System: history of the library','https://www.librarieshawaii.org/about-us/history/history-of-the-library'],W('Hawaiʻi State Library'),['SAH Archipedia: Hawaii State Library','https://sah-archipedia.org/node/11157'],LU],
  brick='?',hours='Mon–Wed and Sat 9–4; Thu 9–7; Fri 11–4'),
